PLACEHOLDER for the bundled Core ML MNIST digit classifier.

This file is intentionally a text placeholder so the project structure is
complete on Windows machines (where there is no Xcode/coremlcompiler).

Final file:
  - Name:        DigitClassifier.mlmodel
  - Format:      Core ML 6 (`.mlpackage` preferred for iOS 16+).
  - Input:       28×28 grayscale, OneComponent8 pixel buffer.
                 MNIST canonical: 20×20 centered content + 4 px padding.
                 Strokes WHITE on BLACK background (inverted before inference).
  - Output:      Class label "0".."9" with confidence. Class "0" is treated
                 as `.unrecognized` (Sudoku has no 0).
  - Size:        ~200–800 KB.
  - Latency:     <5 ms on A15 Neural Engine.
  - Compute:     `MLModelConfiguration.computeUnits = .cpuAndNeuralEngine`.

Training recipe (recommended in test-plan/06-stylus-sensors-privacy-review.md
§3):
  Datasets:
    - MNIST (60k samples) — baseline.
    - EMNIST-digits (240k samples) — broader handwriting variety.
    - Chars74K (subset) — adds slant/serif diversity.
    - Custom PencilKit-style strokes (1k samples) — matches our actual
      input texture so the model sees real PencilKit ink rendering.
  Augmentations:
    - Rotation ±15°
    - Scale ±20%
    - Stroke-thickness jitter (1–4 px)
  Target accuracy:
    - en-US:    ≥ 92% on Sudoku fixture
    - en-GB/de-DE: ≥ 85% (crossed 7, closed-loop 9, hooked 4)

Once trained:
  1. Export as DigitClassifier.mlpackage.
  2. Add to iosApp/iosApp/Models/ in project.yml as a `resource:` reference.
  3. Xcode will auto-generate `DigitClassifier.swift` for typed access.
  4. Wire into StylusInputService.classifyCoreML(...) per its TODO comment.

References:
  - Core ML overview:        https://developer.apple.com/documentation/coreml
  - Vision + Core ML:        https://developer.apple.com/documentation/vision/vncoremlrequest
  - MNIST_DRAW example:      https://github.com/hwchong/MNIST_DRAW
  - MNIST-CoreML example:    https://github.com/ph1ps/MNIST-CoreML
